    <statement><p>The temperature adjusted for wind-chill, <m>w</m>, is a temperature which
tells you how cold it feels, as a result of the combination of wind and
temperature [see
<url href="">wind-chill</url>].
See the table below, which gives temperature adjusted for wind-chill,
<m>w</m>, as a function of temperature <m>T</m> and wind speed <m>s</m>.</p>
